# Assignment 3: Writing Programs Using Your Custom ISA

## 1. Objective

To validate the design of our "NPU" Accelerator by implementing three functional programs using the custom Instruction Set Architecture (ISA) defined in Deliverable 1. These programs demonstrate arithmetic capability, control flow (loops), and reusable function calls.

---

## 2. Tasks & Code

### A. Program 1 — Basic Arithmetic & Memory

#### Description:
This program demonstrates vector arithmetic and memory operations. It loads two vectors (A and B) from memory, computes the result V_result = (A + B) * A, and stores the final vector back to memory.

#### Assembly Code:

```assembly
# ==========================================
# PROGRAM 1: Basic Vector Arithmetic
# ==========================================
.text
.globl main
main:
    # --- 1. Setup Memory Addresses ---
    # x10 = Address of Vector A (0x100 = 256)
    ADDI x10, x0, 256
    
    # x11 = Address of Vector B (0x200 = 512)
    ADDI x11, x0, 512
    
    # x12 = Address for Result (0x300 = 768)
    ADDI x12, x0, 768
    
    # --- 2. Load Data from Memory ---
    # Load 4 integers (128-bits) from Mem[x10] into V1
    VLOAD V1, 0(x10)
    
    # Load 4 integers from Mem[x11] into V2
    VLOAD V2, 0(x11)
    
    # --- 3. Perform Calculation ---
    # Step A: Add Vectors (V3 = V1 + V2)
    VADD V3, V1, V2
    
    # Step B: Multiply Result by Vector A (V3 = V3 * V1)
    VMUL V3, V3, V1
    
    # --- 4. Store Result ---
    # Store the final vector V3 back to memory at address 0x300
    VSTORE V3, 0(x12)
    
    # End of Program 1
    NOP
```

#### Instruction Encoding Table:

| Instruction | Format | Opcode | Funct3 | Funct7 | Hex Encoding |
|-------------|--------|--------|--------|---------|--------------|
| VLOAD V1, 0(x10) | I-Type | 1110111 | 111 | No bits | 0x000570F7 |
| VLOAD V2, 0(x11) | I-Type | 1110111 | 111 | No bits | 0x0005F177 |
| VADD V3, V1, V2 | R-Type | 1110111 | 000 | 0000000 | 0x002081F7 |
| VMUL V3, V3, V1 | R-Type | 1110111 | 010 | 0000000 | 0x0011A1F7 |
| VSTORE V3, 0(x12) | S-Type | 1110111 | 111 | No bits | 0x00367077 |

